+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

The shfmt command uses pledge(2) before reading source files or
EditorConfig settings. In-place editing with -w also permits creating,
replacing and setting permissions on output files. The command exits if
it cannot install the policy.

The policy permits reading input and configuration paths and using
inherited file descriptors. The parsing library leaves the policy of an
embedding application to its caller.
